-<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>deployment-and-ops</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=20260922"></head><body><nav><h1><a href="README.html">Sonuvi documentation</a></h1><div class="meta">Canonical source: <code>docs/wiki-source/</code></div><details><summary><strong>Start</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="README.html">README</a></li><li><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a></li><li><a href="using-now-playing.html">Using Sonuvi</a></li><li><a href="core-concepts.html">Core Concepts</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Displays</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="displays.html">Displays</a></li><li><a href="user-interfaces.html">User Interfaces</a></li><li><a href="kiosk-interface.html">Kiosk</a></li><li><a href="visualizer-in-embedded-mode.html">Visualizer</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Playback and Library</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="playback-features.html">Playback Features</a></li><li><a href="queue-and-playback-model.html">Queue and Playback</a></li><li><a href="queue-wizard-internals.html">Queue Wizard</a></li><li><a href="media-library.html">Media Library</a></li><li><a href="listen-on-device.html">Listen on Device</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Integrations</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="integrations.html">Integrations</a></li><li><a href="alexa-interface.html">Alexa</a></li><li><a href="youtube-interface.html">YouTube</a></li><li><a href="radio-interface.html">Radio</a></li><li><a href="mabel-integration.html">Mabel</a></li><li><a href="jukebox-priority-model.html">Jukebox Priority</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Administration</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="configuration-and-administration.html">Configuration and Administration</a></li><li><a href="config-interface.html">Config</a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">Diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">Deployment and Ops</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Developer Reference</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="developer-reference.html">Developer Reference</a></li><li><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a></li><li><a href="api-service-overview.html">API Overview</a></li><li><a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">API Catalog</a></li><li><a href="source-map.html">Source Map</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Troubleshooting and Maintenance</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="troubleshooting-and-technical-notes.html">Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="playback-issue-triage-runbook.html">Playback Triage</a></li><li><a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html">Display Triage</a></li><li><a href="documentation-sources-audit.html">Documentation Audit</a></li><li><a href="wiki-operations.html">Wiki Operations</a></li></ul></details></nav><article><h1>deployment and ops</h1><h2>Purpose</h2><p>This page explains how changes in <code>now-playing</code> actually become live.</p><p>It should answer: what did I change, which machine or process does that affect, does it usually need only refresh/verification or also restart, and what should I verify afterward?</p><h2>The main operational lesson</h2><blockquote><p>A change can succeed at one layer and still fail to produce the effect you actually care about.</p></blockquote><p>Examples: an endpoint can return success while the moOde display target did not change; a page can look right in a normal browser but still be wrong in kiosk or embedded mode; config can be saved while startup-captured behavior has not changed yet.</p><h2>The system has more than one operational plane</h2><h3>1. App host plane</h3><p>Owns API routes, served UI, controller/display pages, state-truth endpoints like <code>/now-playing</code>, and queue/playback mediation logic.</p><h3>2. moOde host effect plane</h3><p>Owns visible display-target results, browser-target switching, and some runtime/display effects triggered through control-plane routes.</p><h3>3. Host override plane</h3><p>Owns manual or mirrored host-side override material outside the normal app tree.</p><h2>Change type → effect → verify</h2><h3>If you changed a browser page or frontend-only asset</h3><p>Examples: <code>controller.html</code>, <code>app.html</code>, <code>kiosk.html</code>, <code>visualizer.html</code>, CSS, browser-side JS.</p><p>Usually means: app-host served files changed; refresh is often enough; API restart is often unnecessary if the change is truly frontend-only.</p><p>But you still must verify the real operating context: normal, embedded, kiosk, or moOde-pushed target.</p><h3>If you changed route logic or service logic</h3><p>Examples: <code>src/routes/*.mjs</code>, service helpers, <code>moode-nowplaying-api.mjs</code>.</p><p>Usually means: app-host behavior changed, route verification should come first, and restart may be needed depending on how the process loads the code.</p><h3>If you changed runtime-admin behavior</h3><p>Examples: <code>/config/runtime/*</code>, <code>/config/moode/*</code>, <code>/config/services/*</code>.</p><p>Usually means: you changed control-plane behavior that may affect the app host, the moOde host, or both. Verify the actual target effect, not only the response.</p><h3>If you changed a state-truth endpoint</h3><p>Examples: <code>/now-playing</code>, <code>/next-up</code>, Alexa state helpers.</p><p>Usually means: you changed one of the system’s central truth surfaces. Verify the endpoint first, then verify the dependent surfaces.</p><h3>If you changed a host override or host-side patch</h3><p>Usually means: normal app deploy assumptions are not enough. Verify the real host state and the real effect on that host.</p><h2>App host vs moOde host: the key question</h2><p>When something changed and the visible system still looks wrong, ask: <strong>Which machine should have changed?</strong></p><ul><li><strong>App host:</strong> route changed, served page changed, <code>/now-playing</code> output changed, controller/kiosk logic changed</li><li><strong>moOde host:</strong> browser target changed, room-facing display switched, host-side display/runtime action took effect</li></ul><h2>Restart reality</h2><p>Not every change needs restart, but route/service/startup-captured behavior is more restart-sensitive than page-only changes.</p><p>For more detailed restart reasoning, use <a href="restart-and-runtime-admin-troubleshooting.html">restart-and-runtime-admin-troubleshooting</a> and <a href="backend-change-verification-runbook.html">backend-change-verification-runbook</a>.</p><h2>What to verify after common change types</h2><h3>Example: changed <code>controller.html</code></h3><p>Likely effect: app-host-served UI changed. Verify the real controller/kiosk context, not only a generic browser load.</p><h3>Example: changed <code>visualizer.html</code></h3><p>Likely effect: visualizer engine behavior changed. Verify fullscreen, embedded, and push-to-moOde behavior if relevant.</p><h3>Example: changed <code>moode-nowplaying-api.mjs</code></h3><p>Likely effect: state-truth endpoint behavior changed. Verify the endpoint directly, then verify downstream controller/display surfaces.</p><h3>Example: changed <code>config.runtime-admin.routes.mjs</code></h3><p>Likely effect: runtime-admin/control-plane behavior changed. Verify both endpoint response and real target effect.</p><h3>Example: changed moOde-side override material</h3><p>Likely effect: host behavior changed outside the normal app tree. Verify live host state, not just mirrored repo content.</p><h2>What this page is really teaching</h2><ul><li>there is more than one operational plane in the project</li><li>app host and moOde host should not be mentally collapsed</li><li>different change types become live in different ways</li><li>the first verification question is often “what layer should have changed?”</li><li>successful response, served file, and visible effect are three different things</li></ul><h2>Current status</h2><p>This page should now be read as a practical change-type → effect → verify guide, not an abstract ops summary.</p></article><script>(function(){var path=(location.pathname.split('/').pop()||'README.html');document.querySelectorAll('nav a[href]').forEach(function(a){var href=a.getAttribute('href');if(href===path){a.classList.add('nav-current');var details=a.closest('details');if(details) details.open=true;}});})();</script><script>(function(){const input=document.getElementById('nav-search');const results=document.getElementById('nav-search-results');const data=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_INDEX;if(!input||!results||!data)return;const entries=Array.isArray(data)?data:Object.entries(data).map(([path,text])=>({path,title:path.replace(/\.html$/,''),text:String(text||'')}));function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[c]||c));}function search(q){q=q.toLowerCase();return entries.map(e=>{const hay=((e.title||'')+' '+(e.path||'')+' '+(e.text||'')).toLowerCase();if(!hay.includes(q))return null;let score=0;if((e.title||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))score+=8;if((e.path||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))score+=5;score+=Math.max(1,Math.min(3,hay.split(q).length-1));return {score,...e};}).filter(Boolean).sort((a,b)=>b.score-a.score).slice(0,8);}input.addEventListener('input',()=>{const q=input.value.trim();if(!q){results.style.display='none';results.innerHTML='';return;}const found=search(q);results.style.display='block';if(!found.length){results.innerHTML='<div class="meta">No matches.</div>';return;}results.innerHTML=found.map(e=>'<div style="margin:.35rem 0"><a href="'+esc(e.path)+'">'+esc(e.title)+'</a><div class="meta">'+esc((e.text||'').slice(0,120))+'...</div></div>').join('');});})();</script></body></html>
