-<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>diagnostics-interface</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=20260922"><script src="search-index.js?v=20260922"></script></head><body><nav><h1><a href="README.html">Sonuvi documentation</a></h1><div class="meta">Canonical source: <code>docs/wiki-source/</code></div><details><summary><strong>Start</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="README.html">README</a></li><li><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a></li><li><a href="using-now-playing.html">Using Sonuvi</a></li><li><a href="core-concepts.html">Core Concepts</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Displays</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="displays.html">Displays</a></li><li><a href="user-interfaces.html">User Interfaces</a></li><li><a href="kiosk-interface.html">Kiosk</a></li><li><a href="visualizer-in-embedded-mode.html">Visualizer</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Playback and Library</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="playback-features.html">Playback Features</a></li><li><a href="queue-and-playback-model.html">Queue and Playback</a></li><li><a href="queue-wizard-internals.html">Queue Wizard</a></li><li><a href="media-library.html">Media Library</a></li><li><a href="listen-on-device.html">Listen on Device</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Integrations</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="integrations.html">Integrations</a></li><li><a href="alexa-interface.html">Alexa</a></li><li><a href="youtube-interface.html">YouTube</a></li><li><a href="radio-interface.html">Radio</a></li><li><a href="mabel-integration.html">Mabel</a></li><li><a href="jukebox-priority-model.html">Jukebox Priority</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Administration</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="configuration-and-administration.html">Configuration and Administration</a></li><li><a href="config-interface.html">Config</a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">Diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">Deployment and Ops</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Developer Reference</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="developer-reference.html">Developer Reference</a></li><li><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a></li><li><a href="api-service-overview.html">API Overview</a></li><li><a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">API Catalog</a></li><li><a href="source-map.html">Source Map</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Troubleshooting and Maintenance</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="troubleshooting-and-technical-notes.html">Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="playback-issue-triage-runbook.html">Playback Triage</a></li><li><a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html">Display Triage</a></li><li><a href="documentation-sources-audit.html">Documentation Audit</a></li><li><a href="wiki-operations.html">Wiki Operations</a></li></ul></details></nav><article><h1>diagnostics interface</h1><h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2><p>This page documents <code>now-playing/diagnostics.html</code>, the diagnostics and live-inspection console in the <code>now-playing</code> ecosystem.</p><p>This page is intentionally implementation-aware, because <code>diagnostics.html</code> is clearly not just a passive status screen. It acts as a multi-purpose operator console for making direct API requests, inspecting responses, testing endpoints with or without <code>x-track-key</code>, viewing live embedded UI surfaces side-by-side, and navigating operational/debug workflows through a browser UI.</p><h2 id="why-this-page-matters">Why this page matters</h2><p><code>diagnostics.html</code> appears to be one of the strongest operator-facing truth surfaces in the project. It combines direct endpoint execution, live embedded views of multiple UI surfaces, clipboard/curl-oriented debugging helpers, and quick comparison between API behavior and rendered UI behavior.</p><h2 id="important-files">Important files</h2><ul><li>Primary page: <code>now-playing/diagnostics.html</code></li><li>Important supporting script: <code>now-playing/scripts/diagnostics.js</code></li></ul><p>Related pages include <a href="configuration-and-diagnostics-interfaces.html"><code>configuration-and-diagnostics-interfaces.md</code></a>, <a href="config-interface.html"><code>config-interface.md</code></a>, <a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html"><code>display-surface-troubleshooting.md</code></a>, and <a href="deployment-and-ops.html"><code>deployment-and-ops.md</code></a>.</p><h2 id="high-level-role">High-level role</h2><p>A good current interpretation is that <code>diagnostics.html</code> is a browser-based operator/debug console, helps bridge raw API behavior and visible UI behavior, and is one of the most practical pages for side-by-side inspection and debugging.</p><h2 id="shell-entry-behavior">Shell / entry behavior</h2><p>Like <code>config.html</code>, <code>diagnostics.html</code> contains shell-redirect behavior: if <code>standalone=1</code>, remain standalone; if top-level without standalone, redirect into <code>app.html?page=diagnostics.html</code>; if embedded in another shell already, do not redirect.</p><h2 id="major-ui-areas-visible-in-the-page">Major UI areas visible in the page</h2><h3>1. Request runner / endpoint console</h3><p>This top card includes endpoint filtering/selection, method selection, path field, JSON body field for POST, run button, favorite toggle, copy-as-curl button, copy-response button, optional <code>send x-track-key</code> checkbox, and a status area.</p><h3>2. Live embedded view cards</h3><p>The page includes multiple live embedded-view cards for direct UI inspection, including live now-playing view, live player view, live peppy skin view, live controller view, and live kiosk view.</p><h2 id="important-dom-action-centers">Important DOM/action centers</h2><p>Observed important elements include request-runner controls like <code>#endpointFilter</code>, <code>#endpoint</code>, <code>#method</code>, <code>#path</code>, <code>#body</code>, <code>#runBtn</code>, <code>#favBtn</code>, <code>#copyCurlBtn</code>, <code>#useTrackKey</code>, <code>#copyBtn</code>, and <code>#status</code>, plus live-view frames and their reload/toggle/zoom controls.</p><h2 id="diagnostics-script-as-the-logic-center">Diagnostics script as the logic center</h2><p>The main page includes <code>scripts/diagnostics.js</code>, which strongly suggests most of the request-running, favorites, frame-management, and interaction logic lives there rather than inline.</p><h2 id="anatomy-companion-page">Anatomy companion page</h2><p><a href="diagnostics-page-anatomy.html"><code>diagnostics-page-anatomy.md</code></a></p><p>This is the anatomy-style companion page for <code>diagnostics.html</code>. Use it when the task is not just about Diagnostics as a surface, but about a specific region such as the request runner, favorites/endpoint selector, track-key toggle, curl/response helper layer, or embedded live-surface cards.</p><h2 id="request-runner-behavior">Request-runner behavior</h2><p>Based on visible structure, the request runner supports selecting or filtering known endpoints, choosing method, editing path manually, submitting JSON for POST requests, optionally attaching <code>x-track-key</code>, copying equivalent curl, and favoriting endpoints.</p><h2 id="track-key-aware-diagnostics">Track-key-aware diagnostics</h2><p>The diagnostics page includes <code>#useTrackKey</code>, implying the console is designed to test both open/unprotected behavior and protected/track-key-backed behavior.</p><h2 id="live-embedded-surface-inspection">Live embedded-surface inspection</h2><p>This is one of the strongest and most distinctive aspects of <code>diagnostics.html</code>. The page supports a workflow like: run or inspect an endpoint, observe the live rendered result in one or more surfaces, compare whether the API and the UI agree, then reload or reopen affected views quickly.</p><h2 id="relationship-to-display-and-controller-debugging">Relationship to display and controller debugging</h2><p>Because diagnostics embeds multiple live UI surfaces, it sits at the junction of config/diagnostics/admin, display surfaces, controller surfaces, kiosk behavior, and peppy/player render behavior.</p><h2 id="current-observed-api-config-contact">Current observed API/config contact</h2><p>Even from the current light inspection, we can already see that <code>diagnostics.html</code> fetches runtime config from <code>/config/runtime</code>, conditionally hides/shows some navigation based on runtime config, and is designed to execute arbitrary configured diagnostic requests through the request-runner UI.</p><h2 id="architectural-interpretation">Architectural interpretation</h2><p>A good current interpretation is that <code>diagnostics.html</code> is the browser operator’s live debugging dashboard. It combines API-console behavior with live surface monitoring and is one of the most direct pages for checking whether data flow and rendered UI are aligned.</p><h2 id="related-branch-pages">Related branch pages</h2><ul><li><a href="radio-metadata-eval-interface.html"><code>radio-metadata-eval-interface.md</code></a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-page-anatomy.html"><code>diagnostics-page-anatomy.md</code></a></li></ul><p><code>diagnostics-page-anatomy.md</code> matters when the real question is not only “what is <code>diagnostics.html</code>?” but “which region inside <code>diagnostics.html</code> actually owns the thing I need to change?”</p><h2 id="things-still-to-verify">Things still to verify</h2><p>Future deeper verification should clarify the exact endpoint catalog and grouping inside <code>scripts/diagnostics.js</code>, how favorites are stored and restored, how curl-copy generation is implemented, whether the request runner can safely target all important protected endpoints, how the live embedded cards are initialized and refreshed, and whether diagnostics includes hidden/advanced features not visible from markup alone.</p><h2 id="current-status">Current status</h2><p>At the moment, this page already has enough evidence to be treated as one of the project’s core operator/debugging surfaces. It is not just a diagnostics readout; it is a live API console plus multi-surface inspection dashboard, which makes it especially valuable for real troubleshooting work.</p><script>(function(){const input=document.getElementById('nav-search');if(!input)return;const results=document.getElementById('nav-search-results');const details=[...document.querySelectorAll('nav details')];const initialOpen=new Map(details.map(d=>[d,d.open]));const searchIndex=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_INDEX||{};const summaries=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_SUMMARIES||{};const headings=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_HEADINGS||{};const headingTargets=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_HEADING_TARGETS||{};function normalizedTextFor(li){const link=li.querySelector('a');const href=link?link.getAttribute('href')||'':'';const visible=(li.textContent||'').toLowerCase();const indexed=(searchIndex[href]||'').toLowerCase();const summary=(summaries[href]||'').toLowerCase();const headingText=(headings[href]||'').toLowerCase();return {href,visible,indexed,summary,headingText,combined:`${visible} ${indexed} ${summary} ${headingText}`.trim()};}function escapeHtml(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,m=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[m]));}function bestHeadingTarget(href,q){const targets=headingTargets[href]||[];return targets.find(t=>String(t.text||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))||null;}function matchSnippet(meta,q){const target=bestHeadingTarget(meta.href,q);if(target) return {href:`${meta.href}#${target.id}`,text:`Heading match: ${target.text}`};if(meta.summary.includes(q)) return {href:meta.href,text:`Summary match: ${meta.summary}`};if(meta.indexed.includes(q)) return {href:meta.href,text:`Topic match: ${meta.indexed}`};return {href:meta.href,text:`Page match: ${meta.visible}`};}function renderResults(q,matches){if(!results)return;if(!q){results.style.display='none';results.innerHTML='';return;}if(!matches.length){results.style.display='block';results.innerHTML='<div><strong>No direct matches.</strong></div><div style="opacity:.8;margin-top:.3rem">Try a broader term like endpoint, track key, curl, peppy, or kiosk.</div>';return;}const top=matches.slice(0,8).map(({href,label,snippet})=>`<li style="margin:.35rem 0"><a href="${href}"><strong>${escapeHtml(label)}</strong></a><div style="font-size:.9em;opacity:.8">${escapeHtml(snippet)}</div></li>`).join('');results.style.display='block';results.innerHTML=`<div style="margin-bottom:.35rem"><strong>Best matches</strong></div><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem">${top}</ul>`;}function apply(){const q=input.value.trim().toLowerCase();const matches=[];details.forEach(d=>{let any=false;d.querySelectorAll('li').forEach(li=>{const meta=normalizedTextFor(li);const show=!q||meta.combined.includes(q);li.style.display=show?'':'none';if(show)any=true;if(q&&show){const matched=matchSnippet(meta,q);matches.push({href:matched.href,label:(li.textContent||'').trim(),snippet:matched.text});}});d.style.display=any||!q?'':'none';d.open=q?any:initialOpen.get(d);});renderResults(q,matches);}input.addEventListener('input',apply);})();</script></article><script>(function(){var path=(location.pathname.split('/').pop()||'README.html');document.querySelectorAll('nav a[href]').forEach(function(a){var href=a.getAttribute('href');if(href===path){a.classList.add('nav-current');var details=a.closest('details');if(details) details.open=true;}});})();</script><script>(function(){const input=document.getElementById('nav-search');const results=document.getElementById('nav-search-results');const data=window.NP_KNOWLEDGE_SEARCH_INDEX;if(!input||!results||!data)return;const entries=Array.isArray(data)?data:Object.entries(data).map(([path,text])=>({path,title:path.replace(/\.html$/,''),text:String(text||'')}));function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[c]||c));}function search(q){q=q.toLowerCase();return entries.map(e=>{const hay=((e.title||'')+' '+(e.path||'')+' '+(e.text||'')).toLowerCase();if(!hay.includes(q))return null;let score=0;if((e.title||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))score+=8;if((e.path||'').toLowerCase().includes(q))score+=5;score+=Math.max(1,Math.min(3,hay.split(q).length-1));return {score,...e};}).filter(Boolean).sort((a,b)=>b.score-a.score).slice(0,8);}input.addEventListener('input',()=>{const q=input.value.trim();if(!q){results.style.display='none';results.innerHTML='';return;}const found=search(q);results.style.display='block';if(!found.length){results.innerHTML='<div class="meta">No matches.</div>';return;}results.innerHTML=found.map(e=>'<div style="margin:.35rem 0"><a href="'+esc(e.path)+'">'+esc(e.title)+'</a><div class="meta">'+esc((e.text||'').slice(0,120))+'...</div></div>').join('');});})();</script></body></html>
