ct live queue semantics</h2><p>Qobuz Connect is a separate remote playback target exposed through the bearer-authenticated <code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect/queue</code> contract. Its <code>currentIndex</code> addresses the current queue together with <code>upcoming</code>; the <code>history</code> array is recent-first playback context and may include entries retained from before a queue replacement. Therefore <code>history.count</code> may be greater than <code>currentIndex</code> and is not a valid reason to discard the current queue projection or report that PiBuZ ownership is unavailable.</p><p>Saved Qobuz queues use the same mobile session and are server-owned. List and detail are available without an active Connect session; capture requires a fresh <code>confirmed-active</code> ownership proof and a stable cursor; play requires explicit confirmation and status-only polling through the typed operation route. The server preserves ordered occurrences and duplicate positions.</p><p>The current Qobuz control and handoff contract is:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Route</th><th>Required optimistic/confirmation data</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect</code> or <code>/queue</code></td><td>bearer session; snapshot/queue is read-only and source-aware</td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect/{play,resume,pause,next,previous}</code></td><td><code>qobuzTrackId</code> for the current track where required; the server rejects stale or unconfirmed ownership</td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect/seek</code></td><td>current <code>qobuzTrackId</code> and <code>positionSec</code></td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect/queue/jump</code></td><td><code>index</code>, <code>targetQobuzTrackId</code>, <code>queueFingerprint</code>, expected current index/count, and <code>shuffle: false</code></td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/v1/mobile/qobuz-connect/release</code></td><td>no Qobuz credential; returns success only after inactive ownership and receiver readiness are confirmed</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The mobile app must not infer Qobuz identity from title, artwork, or a local path. <code>queueFingerprint</code> is an opaque compare-and-swap token, not a track or catalog identity. A failed or unconfirmed release must stop a Home mutation from racing the remote receiver.</p><p>Each catalog-backed local track receives its authoritative MPD sticker rating through <code>rating</code> (<code>0..5</code>) and <code>ratingDisabled: false</code>. The reader is the same server-side <code>getRatingForFile()</code> path used by the web diagnostics queue. An unrated local track therefore returns <code>rating: 0</code> while keeping the stars enabled. Streams, YouTube, podcasts, unsupported items, and queues where the ratings feature is disabled return <code>rating: 0</code> and <code>ratingDisabled: true</code>. The mobile route never calls <code>/rating/current</code>, never derives the value from catalog metadata, and never exposes a file path or MPD song ID.</p><p>Catalog-backed local tracks also receive <code>isFavorite</code> and <code>favoriteDisabled</code> from the same server-side Favorites playlist reader. The native client renders the heart and five-star row directly below the queue track title and writes changes through the bearer catalog-track favorite and rating routes. Streams, YouTube, podcasts, unsupported items, and unavailable favorite readers return <code>isFavorite: false</code> and <code>favoriteDisabled: true</code>.</p><h2 id="artwork">Artwork</h2><p>Queue artwork comes from the Now Playing artwork resolver/cache, not moOde&#x27;s <code>coverart.php</code> or filesystem paths. For local catalog tracks the queue item uses the same bearer-protected <code>/v1/mobile/artwork/:trackId</code> route used by albums, artists, playlists, and playback metadata. Radio/stream rows use the server&#x27;s station-logo fallback. Radio rows