-Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The route requires the existing <code>mobile-api</code> bearer scope. A Track Key alone must receive HTTP 401. The native client never calls <code>/now-playing</code> directly.</p><h2 id="response">Response</h2><pre><code>{
+Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code></pre><p>The route requires the existing <code>mobile-api</code> bearer scope. A Track Key alone must receive HTTP 401. The native client never calls <code>/now-playing</code> directly.</p><p>This is a Server-backed current-state contract. It does not make the current Server catalog permanent: the approved native target is an iOS-device-owned canonical catalog with provider observations and server-independent native playback, but identity merging, enrichment conflict rules, and synchronization contracts for that target are not implemented here. Until those contracts are approved, the client must treat the Server&#x27;s opaque <code>MobileTrack</code> identity and the routes in this page as authoritative for Home playback, metadata, artwork, and history handoff.</p><h2 id="response">Response</h2><pre><code>{
   &quot;ok&quot;: true,
   &quot;available&quot;: true,
   &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Example Track&quot;,
