+<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>mobile-videos</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=20260922"><script src="search-index.js?v=20260922"></script></head><body><nav><h1><a href="README.html">Sonuvi documentation</a></h1><div class="meta">Canonical source: <code>docs/wiki-source/</code></div><details><summary><strong>Start</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="README.html">README</a></li><li><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a></li><li><a href="using-now-playing.html">Using Sonuvi</a></li><li><a href="core-concepts.html">Core Concepts</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Displays</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="displays.html">Displays</a></li><li><a href="user-interfaces.html">User Interfaces</a></li><li><a href="kiosk-interface.html">Kiosk</a></li><li><a href="visualizer-in-embedded-mode.html">Visualizer</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Playback and Library</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="playback-features.html">Playback Features</a></li><li><a href="queue-and-playback-model.html">Queue and Playback</a></li><li><a href="queue-wizard-internals.html">Queue Wizard</a></li><li><a href="media-library.html">Media Library</a></li><li><a href="listen-on-device.html">Listen on Device</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Integrations</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="integrations.html">Integrations</a></li><li><a href="alexa-interface.html">Alexa</a></li><li><a href="youtube-interface.html">YouTube</a></li><li><a href="radio-interface.html">Radio</a></li><li><a href="mabel-integration.html">Mabel</a></li><li><a href="jukebox-priority-model.html">Jukebox Priority</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Administration</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="configuration-and-administration.html">Configuration and Administration</a></li><li><a href="config-interface.html">Config</a></li><li><a href="diagnostics-interface.html">Diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="deployment-and-ops.html">Deployment and Ops</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Developer Reference</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="developer-reference.html">Developer Reference</a></li><li><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a></li><li><a href="api-service-overview.html">API Overview</a></li><li><a href="api-endpoint-catalog.html">API Catalog</a></li><li><a href="source-map.html">Source Map</a></li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Troubleshooting and Maintenance</strong></summary><ul><li><a href="troubleshooting-and-technical-notes.html">Troubleshooting</a></li><li><a href="playback-issue-triage-runbook.html">Playback Triage</a></li><li><a href="display-surface-troubleshooting.html">Display Triage</a></li><li><a href="documentation-sources-audit.html">Documentation Audit</a></li><li><a href="wiki-operations.html">Wiki Operations</a></li></ul></details></nav><article><h1 id="mobile-video-api">Mobile Video API</h1><p>The native Sonuvi app accesses videos through the existing paired mobile session. Video playback is separate from MPD, the music catalog, and every server queue.</p><h2 id="configuration">Configuration</h2><ul><li><code>MOBILE_VIDEO_ROOT</code> — configured video storage root. It defaults to the</li></ul><p>installation&#x27;s <code>PI4_MOUNT_BASE</code>, which is the mounted SSD location.</p><ul><li><code>MOBILE_VIDEO_CATALOG_PATH</code> — protected server-side registry for opaque</li></ul><p>video and folder IDs. It defaults to <code>var/mobile-video-catalog.json</code>.</p><p>The registry assigns random opaque IDs; IDs are not derived from titles or filesystem paths. The API never returns absolute paths.</p><h2 id="routes">Routes</h2><p>All routes require <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;mobile-session-token&gt;</code>.</p><h3 id="get-v1mobilecatalogvideos"><code>GET /v1/mobile/catalog/videos</code></h3><p>Returns schema <code>sonuvi.mobile-video-catalog.v1</code> with bounded pagination:</p><pre><code>GET /v1/mobile/catalog/videos?cursor=&lt;opaque&gt;&amp;limit=&lt;1..100&gt;&amp;folderID=&lt;optional&gt;</code></pre><p>Each item includes <code>videoID</code>, title, filename, optional folder identity, MIME type, format, size, duration when <code>ffprobe</code> can read it, modification time, safe metadata, thumbnail availability, playback availability, and opaque <code>thumbnailURL</code>/<code>mediaURL</code> values. <code>.mp4</code>, <code>.m4v</code>, and <code>.mov</code> are playable. <code>.mkv</code> is listed as unsupported until a verified native playback path exists.</p><h3 id="thumbnail-and-media">Thumbnail and media</h3><ul><li><code>GET /v1/mobile/catalog/videos/:videoID/thumbnail</code> returns a bounded JPEG</li></ul><p>thumbnail generated from the authorized source file.</p><ul><li><code>GET /v1/mobile/catalog/videos/:videoID/media</code> serves the original playable</li></ul><p>file with its stored MIME type and byte-range support (<code>206</code>, <code>Content-Range</code>, and <code>Accept-Ranges</code>). No transcoding is performed.</p><p>Every lookup revalidates the file beneath the configured root and rejects symlink entries and path escapes. A missing or detached root returns <code>503</code> with <code>video storage is unavailable</code>; an individual missing ID returns <code>404</code>. Video routes never add files to MPD or mutate any queue.</p></article><script>(function(){var p=(location.pathname.split("/").pop()||"README.html");document.querySelectorAll("nav a[href]").forEach(function(a){if(a.getAttribute("href")===p){a.classList.add("nav-current");var d=a.closest("details");if(d)d.open=true;}});})();</script><script>(function(){var i=document.getElementById("nav-search");if(!i)return;})();</script></body></html>
